# macOS / darwin-arm64 toolchain fix.  Without this, rules_cc's
# auto-generated `local_config_cc/BUILD` detects the system clang
# without LLD on PATH and emits `link_flags = ["-fuse-ld=ld64.lld:", ...]`
# (note the trailing colon).  Apple clang then rejects with:
#
#   clang: error: invalid linker name in argument '-fuse-ld=ld64.lld:'
#
# Putting brew's llvm bin first on the toolchain-discovery PATH makes
# rules_cc emit a clean `-fuse-ld=ld64.lld` (no trailing colon) AND
# selects the homebrew clang, which accepts the flag.
#
# `--repo_env=PATH=...` is the right knob: it scopes the override to
# repository-rule execution (where rules_cc's auto-detection runs)
# without leaking into action env, so reproducible-build hashes are
# unaffected.
build --repo_env=PATH=/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/bin:/usr/bin:/bin
